@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:68e71dc92ff0bb7750b4992ac4c24f856569c8cd }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Every field of every answer now reads a null as the absent value it is }
~ A null in a model's answer costs that field, not the answer

To handle cases where the model writes `null` where a string was asked for and serde refuses the whole reply.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The README now leads with the seven deterministic commands rather than with extraction }
~ The README now leads with the seven deterministic commands rather than with extraction

To focus on the part that needs no model and is worth someone's time today.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": It also no longer implies `stale` works on a fresh clone }
~ It also no longer implies `stale` works on a fresh clone

To clarify that `stale` reads a corpus, which is written by extraction.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The model-dependent third is listed with what it was measured at, model named, in the same table" }
~ The model-dependent third is listed with what it was measured at, model named, in the same table

To provide transparency about the performance of model-dependent commands.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": So `check` **ships advisory**: it prints findings and exits 0 unless `--strict` }
~ `check` ships advisory: it prints findings and exits 0 unless `--strict`

To acknowledge the limitations of the model's precision and advise caution.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": `extract` is honest about being weak }
~ `extract` is honest about being weak

To disclose the limitations of the extraction process based on measured performance.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "What did work: **two-pass agreement** (170 and 192 flags became 96, and it removed every false flag on a real commit in development), which is why `check` runs two passes by default" }
~ Two-pass agreement is used by default for `check` to remove false flags

To improve the precision of findings by ensuring two independent runs agree.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; a model proposes wording only" }
~ The tool assigns labels, sources and statuses; a model proposes content only

To ensure that the tool maintains control over the integrity of the corpus.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Staleness by item body hash. Reasoning is attached to code identity rather than to line ranges, so a function that moved is not stale and one that changed is" }
~ Staleness is detected by item body hash rather than line ranges

To prevent false positives for functions that have merely moved.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Review as records. Confirming writes an attestation, rejecting writes a withdrawal whose reason unit says why, closing writes a resolution" }
~ Review is recorded as confirmations, withdrawals with reasons, or closures with notes

To maintain a transparent and immutable record of review actions.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`bench` measures the model *you* chose on *your* commits, and every published figure names the model it came from" }
~ `bench` measures the model you chose on your own commits

To allow users to measure and verify the performance of their chosen models.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/856a434cf607.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A cloned corpus is someone else's claim. Units carry the status the tool gave them; read `speculative` as what it says }
~ The tool does not trust a cloned corpus as an established fact

To encourage users to verify claims in the corpus independently.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:68e71dc92ff0bb7750b4992ac4c24f856569c8cd }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Every field of every answer now reads a null as the absent value it is }
~ Every field of every answer now reads a null as the absent value it is

To handle cases where the model writes `null` where a string was asked for, and serde refuses the whole reply.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Rewrites now always end with a newline }
~ Rewrites now always end with a newline

To ensure that the file is correctly handled by both the queue and the hook, which have different methods of appending to the file.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": `stale --json` now includes the `behind` field in JSON output instead of printing it on stdout }
~ `stale --json` now includes the `behind` field in JSON output instead of printing it on stdout

To ensure that `--json` outputs only valid JSON, preventing parsing errors when consuming the JSON output.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A test is added to ensure that every `--json` command produces valid JSON output }
~ A test is added to ensure that every `--json` command produces valid JSON output

To catch future regressions where non-JSON content might be printed with `--json`, ensuring the output remains valid.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if let Some(mut around) = scope {" }
~ The `facts` function now includes an optional `scope` parameter to filter facts based on files, names, or hops

To provide more granular control over which facts are displayed.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.estimate {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now estimates the time required for extraction based on commit size and prints …

To give users an idea of how long the extraction process will take, especially when processing multiple commits.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if dry_run {" }
~ The `extract` function now includes a dry-run mode that simulates the extraction process without actually …

To allow users to preview what would be extracted without making any changes.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if let Some(path) = c.prompt_file {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `prompt_file` parameter that allows specifying a custom system …

To provide more flexibility in how the check process is conducted.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let take = if r.max_commits == 0 {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `max_commits` parameter to limit the number of commits processed

To prevent processing an excessive number of commits at once, which could be resource-intensive.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let kept = if force {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `force` parameter to force re-extraction of already recorded …

To allow users to re-extract commits that have already been recorded.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.dry_run {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `dry_run` parameter to simulate the extraction process without …

To allow users to preview what would be extracted without making any changes.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-24 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.no_corpus_order {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `no_corpus_order` parameter that allows disabling corpus order

To provide more flexibility in how the check process is conducted.

@decision d/g68e71dc92ff0-25 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/f4a0deceb63d.smy@68e71dc92ff0 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`--json` must be JSON, and nothing else." }
~ `--json` must be JSON, and nothing else

CI went red on a corpus that had grown enough for the case to arise: `stale --json` printed which decisions each moved item was behind — on stdout, before the JSON — and anything reading the output got `Expecting value: line 1 column 3`.

